# What this file covers never reaches the published repository, and the
# hooks in .githooks/ hold it to that: the pre-commit hook refuses any path
# matched here (even one forced in with `git add -f`) and the pre-push hook
# checks every outgoing commit again. Turn them on once per clone:
#
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks

# Local working notes, ignored as one directory so a note written there
# tomorrow is covered the day it is written. Ignored means "not published",
# not "disposable": scripts/checkpoint.sh still snapshots all of it.
docs/internal/
# The old home of the working list and some research, moved into
# docs/internal/ on 8 Oct 2026; nothing public is kept here any more.
docs/product/

# Suites that check the local working notes rather than the extension. They
# name files that are themselves ignored, so they stay out of the history too;
# `run-all.js` picks up anything matching this pattern when it is present.
tests/local-*.js

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Temporary files, and probe screenshots dropped at the root
*.tmp
*.temp
/*.png

# Packaged store build artifacts
assets/upload/
*.zip

# Test dependencies (dev-only)
tests/node_modules/
# package-lock.json is deliberately TRACKED: it pins every transitive dev
# dependency to an exact resolved version + integrity hash, which is the only
# real defence against a dependency being hijacked between installs.

# The iPhone app: generated artefacts only — the project comes from
# ios/project.yml, the page from ios/scripts/build-webapp.sh
ios/WebApp/
ios/PriceTab.xcodeproj/
ios/PriceTab/Assets.xcassets/
ios/PriceTabWidget/Assets.xcassets/
ios/build/
ios/DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
